Package: irtident
Type: Package
Title: Practical Identification Diagnostics for Item Response Models Fitted with 'mirt'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", email = "yonggi1124@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Diagnoses which item parameters of a unidimensional, single-group
    item response model fitted with 'mirt' are weakly identified by the data,
    and why. Four complementary diagnostics are provided: (1) item-level local
    diagnostics that split each parameter's sampling variance into an
    intrinsic part and inflation caused by confounding with parameters of the
    same item or of other items; (2) profile likelihood intervals with
    flatness indicators, following the practical identifiability approach of
    Raue et al. (2009) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btp358>; (3) multi-start
    estimation with clustering of the solutions, which separates
    equivalent-fit modes from inferior local optima; and (4) a simulation
    that estimates the sample size needed to recover a given parameter.
    Models are estimated with 'mirt' (Chalmers, 2012) <doi:10.18637/jss.v048.i06>.
